{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-evidence` skill MUST be the home of the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message for a change to agreed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation. Under `requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-evidence` skill must be the home of six topics: the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message. A home topic is stated in full in exactly one skill.\n\nThe only marked test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_is_home_of_authoring_findings_and_assessment_outcomes]`. It covers each topic as follows:\n- **Authoring workflow:** it asserts that the `## Workflow` section of `habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` contains `habeas author --all`.\n- **Fixing findings:** it asserts that `## Fixing findings` contains the `| Finding | Action |` table and the `### Missing test and example references` subsection.\n- **Disagreeing assessments:** it asserts that `## Disagreeing assessments` contains `The goal is`.\n- **Commit message:** it asserts that `## Rules` contains `in the message of the commit that makes it`.\n- **FIXME judgments:** it asserts that `references/fixme.md` contains `# FIXME judgments`.\n- **Citation and site reviews:** it asserts that `references/reviews.md` contains `## Citation reviews` and `## Site reviews`.\n- **Outcomes:** this topic has no direct section assertion. `assert_home` covers it through the marker `A judgment is one of three outcomes` in `home_markers`.\n\nThe `assert_home` helper does two further things:\n- It checks that the evidence skill contains every `home_markers` phrase for `habeas-evidence`. Those phrases cover the outcomes, `habeas author --all`, the `## Fixing findings` heading, the FIXME judgment, the citation review, the built-in and site-judgment rules, the disagreement goal, and the commit-message phrasing.\n- For every other skill in `SKILLS` (`habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `habeas-refactor`), it asserts that the skill does not contain any of those markers. This enforces the 'exactly one skill' exclusivity.\n\nI read the helpers `skill_files`, `skill_md`, `skill_file`, `section`, `assert_text`, `assert_phrases`, `home_markers` and `assert_home`. They include the `references/` files in the skill definition, as the parent requirement specifies. The assertions are real `assert!` calls with the expected phrases.\n\nI found no counterexample the test would accept. If a topic moved out of the evidence skill, its section or marker assertion would fail. If another skill restated a topic marker, `assert_home` would fail. Whether a restatement in different wording would escape is not something the requirement text specifies, so it is not a gap. No acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "705ed82e4b6db789bc1e43ba36e10077d3f5b824870ae00641b8c90ee5333b95",
